# netsurf: a restyled block whose parent is a cell, a float or an inline-block (patch 470)
# Generated 2026-11-27
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 469)
#
# "declined (restyled block's parent is not a block)" -- 5.7 a load on
# the 21-site census (wikipedia, rte, archwiki): html_rl_block_restyle
# takes a block whose parent box is a block, flex or grid box (or the
# root, through 419's walk) and declined on anything else. Logged now
# (the element and its parent box), a probe found:
# - a <div> in a <td> (wikipedia): built again whole where it is, as 434
#   does for a block that is not one line of plain content
#   (html_rl_flex_restyle takes a cell parent; the page is laid out
#   whole, 366);
# - a floated block, its box in an anonymous float box (wikipedia's
#   <button>, rte's <div>), and a block in an inline-block (rte's
#   <app-video-basic>): the nearest block, flex or grid box above is
#   built again whole (456's html_rl_enclosing_whole), which builds the
#   float or the inline-block, its line and everything in it from the DOM.
#   html_rl_flex_restyle's 456 branch takes a float parent the same way
#   (wikipedia's <button>, reached by 434's whole-block rebuild).
# The root (<html>, when 419's walk declines: more than 8 elements
# restyle) keeps the full rebuild.
#
